[size=4]Admin commands[/size]

Type these in the game's console (F5). The server decides who is an admin from its own admin list; anyone else is told no.

[list]
[*][b]wg_list[/b] lists every portal with its owner, who may use it and where it goes.
[*][b]wg_status[/b] shows the version, the protocol number, the portal counts and whether the travel check is on.
[*][b]wg_unlink <portal name>[/b] removes the destination of every portal with that name. Names, owners and sharing stay.
[/list]


[size=4]Versions[/size]

A client and a server run the same protocol or the selection screen says so and stays read-only ("This server runs Portal Network x.y, which this version cannot read"). Newer versions add to the portal list without breaking older ones; the protocol number only changes when something cannot be added that way.


[size=4]Who can use a portal[/size]

On a server, a new portal is private to the player who built it: other players do not see it in their list and cannot link to it or jump through it. The owner decides who else gets in, with the row of buttons under the portal's name in the screen:

[list]
[*][b]EVERYONE[/b] shares it with every player.
[*][b]SHARE WITH[/b] opens a list of everyone who has ever joined the world; click a name to share with that person, click again to take it back. Shares follow the player's account, not the character, and work while they are offline.
[*][b]WARD[/b] lets members of a ward standing over the portal use it (on by default; turn it off to keep them out). Wards belong to characters, so this one follows the character.
[*]Admins see and manage every portal.
[*]A player can point a portal they may use at any other portal they may use, and nowhere else.
[*]Only the owner (and admins) can rename a portal. A portal with no known builder can be renamed by anyone who may use it.
[/list]

Portals that already stood in a world when you added Portal Network stay open to everyone until their owner decides: the first time the owner opens one, a question asks whether to keep it shared or make it private. In a single-player game none of this shows.


[size=4]Settings[/size]

Edit [b]BepInEx/config/com.cartur.portalnetwork.cfg[/b] (or use Configuration Manager). Restart the game after changing a value.

[list]
[*][b]Portal / OpenRange[/b] (default 8): Distance in metres at which a portal with a destination opens. Vanilla uses 5.
[*][b]Portal / PortalZoom[/b] (default on): The camera flies into the portal when you jump, holds a moment on the far portal on arrival, then pulls back out. Off keeps the normal black loading screen.
[*][b]Portal / SoundVolume[/b] (default 0.56): How loud the portal sounds are: opening, hum while open, closing, and the hum while a jump loads. The default is as loud as the vanilla portal hum (measured on the files: -16.1 against -16.2 LUFS); 1 is five decibels above it. They also get quieter with distance, like the vanilla hum.
[*][b]Portal / ArrivalClosedSeconds[/b] (default 10): How long you cannot walk back into the portal you came out of. 0 turns it off.
[*][b]Portal / ArrivalClosedFeet[/b] (default 5): Walk this many feet away from the portal you came out of and you may use it again at once.
[*][b]Portal / Alive[/b] (default 1): How much the opening moves: the edge breathes, the picture ripples, the rune glow pulses. 0 is still.
[*][b]Mist / FloorAmount[/b] (default 0.5): Mist that fans out of the front of the portal along the ground, about a foot deep; wind and people walking through move it. 0 turns it off.
[*][b]Mist / FrameEdgeAmount[/b] (default 0.25): A faint wisp round the inside edge of the frame. 0 turns it off.
[*][b]Passage / AllowAllItems[/b] (default off): Lets ore, metal and every other item vanilla blocks go through any portal.
[*][b]Passage / TakeFollowers[/b] (default off): Tamed animals following you come through the portal with you.
[*][b]Passage / ShortNearbyJump[/b] (default on): Short jumps take about 2 seconds.
[*][b]Passage / ServerTravelCheck[/b] (default on): The server checks a jump before it happens.
[*][b]Menu / FilterNames[/b] (default off): Portal names in the screen go through the game's text filter.
[*][b]Menu / ListOnlyExplored[/b] (default off): The screen lists only portals whose spot is on your map. Off lists every portal in the world. Set by each player for themselves.
[*][b]Menu animation / Enabled[/b] (default on): The frame's light, the opening and closing, and the effects on picking a destination. Off shows a still, lit frame. Also turns off the portal camera flight.
[*][b]Menu animation / FollowWindowsSetting[/b] (default on): When Windows has "Show animations in Windows" switched off (Settings > Accessibility > Visual effects), the menu is still and the portal camera flight is off.
[*][b]Menu animation / Speed[/b] (default 1): How fast the menu animations and the portal camera flight run. 0.5 to 2.
[*][b]Menu animation / AmbientGlow[/b] (default 1.4): How much the frame's light rises and falls while the screen is open. 0 holds it steady. Up to 1.5.
[*][b]Menu animation / HoverGlow[/b] (default 1.4): Strength of the light under a hovered or selected row. 0 is none. Up to 1.5.
[*][b]Menu animation / Streaks[/b] (default 1.4): Strength of the thin light streaks that run out from a row when you pick a destination. 0 is none. Up to 1.5.
[*][b]Menu animation / TravellingLight[/b] (default on): A faint light travels round the frame's carved channels, one circuit about every 8 seconds. Off keeps the channels steady.
[/list]

On a server the four Passage settings are the server's: players joining use the server's values and their own file is not changed. Mist, Alive, OpenRange, PortalZoom, the two Arrival settings, Menu and Menu animation stay with each player.

Even with AllowAllItems on, items vanilla treats as never teleportable (tool tier 1000 and above) are still refused.


[size=4]Compatibility[/size]

[list]
[*]Tested on Valheim 1.0.21 with BepInExPack Valheim 5.4.2351, in single player and on a dedicated server with one player.
[*][b]Not compatible with XPortal.[/b] Portal Network will not load if XPortal is installed, because both change how portals link. Valheim Community Patch's portal-connection fix steps aside when Portal Network is installed (it says so in the log). No other portal mods have been checked; at startup the log names any other mod that patches the same portal code, so a clash shows up there.
[*]On a server, Portal Network must be installed on the server and on every client. Without it on the server, the selection screen shows "the server does not have Portal Network" and jumps work as vanilla.
[/list]


[size=4]Languages[/size]

Text is English only for now. It lives in [b]Translations/English.txt[/b] next to the DLL. To add a language, copy that file, name it after the game's name for the language (for example [b]German.txt[/b]), and translate the part after each [b]=[/b]. A line you leave out shows in English.


[size=4]Known limits[/size]

[list]
[*]During a long jump the picture of the other side is the small one used in the portal's window, shown enlarged. It looks soft at high resolutions.
[*]The portal camera flight does not blur the edges of the picture or split its colours; it widens the view and flashes cyan.
[/list]


[size=4]Not tested yet[/size]

[list]
[*][b]A second real player.[/b] Private and shared portals, shares to offline friends and ward access have only been tried on a dedicated server with one player. Nobody else has joined a server running it.
[*][b]Seeing someone arrive with a real second player.[/b] The server's "someone is arriving" message was sent to a real connected client (it arrived, and was not sent to a client 136 m away or to the traveller), but nobody has watched a real arrival from the side.
[*]Crossplay players (their ids are handled like Steam ids, but this was not tried).
[*]The Hammer's placement screen itself. The piece was placed with the game's placement function and removed through the Hammer's removal call; the cost taken is the game's own.
[*]Controllers and the Steam Deck. The list answers the D-pad or left stick (move), A (choose), X (disconnect), Y (sort) and B (close), but no controller has been tried. Ultrawide screens have not been tried either.
[*]The Windows "Show animations in Windows" switch actually turned off, and the [b]Speed[/b] setting.
[*]Languages other than English.
[*]A jump through a portal that has no picture of the other side yet.
[*]Taking tamed animals through with a follow command from other mods, more than two animals at a time, or animals owned by another player.
[/list]


[size=4]Install and uninstall[/size]

Install with a mod manager, or copy [b]CarturPortalNetwork.dll[/b] and [b]portalnetwork.bundle[/b] into [b]BepInEx/plugins/CarturPortalNetwork/[/b].

To remove it: delete that folder. Before you do, take down any Network portals you built, since they will not exist without the mod. Once the mod is gone, the game links portals by name only. Every link you made on the selection screen is lost. Portals that share a name get paired with each other in an order nobody controls, so with three or more of the same name some of them end up joined to the wrong one, and a portal whose name no other portal has goes nowhere. Before you remove the mod, give each pair of portals you want to keep its own matching name, and give every other portal a name that nothing else uses.


